# Platform-injected on deploy. Copy to .env locally if needed — never commit secrets.
# DATABASE_URL=
# BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=
# BETTER_AUTH_URL=
# GROK_AUTH_CLIENT_ID=
# GROK_AUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GROK_PREVIEW_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=           From this app's OWN Google Cloud OAuth client
#                             (Console -> APIs & Services -> Credentials),
#                             NOT the broker's. Used for native Google
#                             sign-in in production/local dev
#                             (src/lib/auth/server.ts's socialProviders) --
#                             the live-preview sandbox still uses the
#                             broker (GROK_AUTH_*) instead, since only that
#                             solves the preview iframe's partitioned
#                             cookies. Google Console's Authorized redirect
#                             URI must be exactly
#                             `${BETTER_AUTH_URL}/api/auth/callback/google`.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=       Paired with GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID above. Absent
#                             entirely (not merely disabled) when either of
#                             this pair is unset -- src/lib/auth/server.ts
#                             only spreads `socialProviders.google` into the
#                             Better Auth config when both are present, so
#                             an unconfigured deploy never renders a Google
#                             button that can't actually complete a sign-in.
# XAI_API_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=      whsec_... from the Stripe Dashboard's webhook
#                             endpoint config (src/routes/api/webhooks/
#                             stripe.ts). Required at runtime -- the endpoint
#                             fails closed (500) without it rather than
#                             accepting unverified deliveries. After setting
#                             it, send a test event from the Stripe
#                             Dashboard's webhook page and confirm a
#                             billing_event row actually appears (see
#                             docs/commerce-launch-checklist.md) -- a wrong
#                             value fails signature verification silently,
#                             with no error a parent would ever see.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=          sk_... Used at runtime by checkout.session.
#                             completed's handler to fetch the just-created
#                             subscription and read its price id (Checkout
#                             Session webhook payloads don't include line
#                             items inline). Kept as a separate env var from
#                             STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET on purpose -- one signs
#                             deliveries, the other authenticates outbound
#                             API calls, and the two must never be confused.
# STRIPE_PRICE_MONTHLY_ID=    price_... the monthly plan's Price id from the
#                             Stripe Dashboard (Product catalog), NOT the
#                             ¥1,280 amount and not a Payment Link id.
#                             src/lib/stripe-plan.ts matches on this id, not
#                             on price -- an amount changing in Stripe no
#                             longer needs a matching code change.
# STRIPE_PRICE_ANNUAL_ID=     price_... same, for the ¥10,800 annual plan.
